  eliminated: 7 of 9.  survivors: ['FREE-LABEL, ell=3', 'm13 singleton triangle']
  the survivors are exactly the models whose palettes are singletons (|A u B| = 2,
  |T'| = 4 >= 3): they are consistent with the mechanism, and a 6-cycle centre
  has no singleton palette (Lemma 3 of sprint/k6/STRUCTURE.md).

================================================================================
D. the mechanism is strictly stronger than the gamma criterion
================================================================================
  direction sets E_A = (0,120), E_B = (120,240) degrees:
    neither contains a full 120-degree orbit, so no gamma witness exists;
    the arc-sum lemma gives a disc of radius >= delta*sigma - delta^2 = 0.717177
    and 1/sqrt3 = 0.577350  =>  disc contains a unit triangle:  True
